      <span class="proj-board">ESP32-C3 &middot; RISC-V</span>
      <p class="proj-status">Complete</p>
      <h2>How Numbers Behave on a Chip With No FPU</h2>
      <p class="proj-dek">Checking the claims against real silicon.</p>
      <p class="summary">
        An investigation that turns each claim about machine arithmetic into a
        tiny on-board probe and reads the verdict off the serial port. Floats
        are torn apart bit by bit, pushed off both edges into infinity and the
        subnormals, and set against integers and fixed-point, on a RISC-V chip
        with no floating-point unit, where every quirk shows plainly. A
        companion to Unit 1 of The Mathematics ML Runs On.
      </p>
      <div class="proj-tags">
        <span>C</span><span>IEEE-754</span><span>Fixed-point</span><span>Undefined behaviour</span>
      </div>
